# Memory-pipeline-fix — Stop hook re-seating + retrieval visibility + group_id convention

2026-04-29. Closes the five-fix bundle the diagnostic agent surfaced
2026-04-29 (`.scratch/claude-output/stop-hook-and-retrieval-
diagnostic.md`). LAST PRE-PUBLISH BLOCKER per dispatcher directive
2026-05-01.

1. **Stop hook never registered in pos3** (Surface 1). Pos3's
   first-run completed 2026-04-23 16:23 UTC; hooks.Stop was never
   merged because `_maybe_merge_stop` only fires from
   `first_run_helper.py`'s first-run-only Phase 3d / Phase 4c /
   Phase 6 paths. Empirical proof: 0 Stop firings vs 68 UPS
   firings vs 2 SessionStart firings in the active session jsonl;
   no `.pos/memory-write-queue/`, no `.pos/memory-writes.log`, no
   `.pos/last-turn-id` in the workspace tree.
   Fix: `pos_session_start.py` gains `_maybe_reseat_stop_hook`
   helper that mirrors the existing `_maybe_install_status_line`
   shape (amendment #49 D5 precedent) — supervisor-path retrofit
   calls `_maybe_merge_stop` on every session-start. Idempotent
   per existing `test_AC_M_11_merge_stop_re_merge_pos_v2_owned.py`.

2. **Retrieval contributor's empty-state path was silent**
   (Surface 2c). `_render_retrieval` returned `""` when
   `result["results"]` was empty, producing the
   `[memory-retrieval]\n    \n` whitespace shape in UPS hook
   attachment (which the diagnostic identified empirically).
   Fix: return `"[memory-retrieval]\n  (no results for this
   query)"` — the empty-state is now observable per M6c
   graceful-fallthrough-with-detection CDC.

3. **Retrieval contributor swallowed exceptions silently**
   (Surface 2c). `try/except: return ""` at memory_consumer.py:256-
   261 left no read-side observability surface.
   Fix: add `_append_diag(workspace_root, exception, query)`
   helper that writes one NDJSON line to
   `<workspace>/.pos/memory-reads.log` with exception type +
   slug + query preview. Mirror of write-side `memory-writes.log`
   per M6c CDC.

4. **Cosmetic dead-code drop** (Surface 2c). Once Fix #2 lands,
   the `or [""]` fallback in `context_composer._serialise_turn`
   at lines 543-546 is dead code for the memory-retrieval path.
   Fix: skip empty contributors in `_serialise_turn` (and skip
   the `contributor_outputs:` header itself when no contributor
   produced text). Cleaner than emitting whitespace-padded
   contributor headers.

5. **Write/read group_id convention alignment** (Surface 2a).
   Diagnostic found 3 episodes in kuzu under `group_id=
   "pos-v2_default"` (memory-system's `default_scope_id` per
   `memory.yml:72`); persona's read path queries with `group_ids=
   [workspace_slug]=["pos3"]`. The persona's write path ALREADY
   writes with `group_id=workspace_slug` (per
   `memory_consumer.py:183`); the orphan `pos-v2_default` data is
   verification-scaffolding from a different path (likely
   amendment #74 verification) and is accepted as lost. No
   source change required — the alignment is already in place.
   Fix: explicit AC + regression-prevention pytest +
   documentation of the convention in module docstring.

The five fixes ship as one amendment because (a) they share the
Stop-hook-not-firing root cause-cluster, (b) Fix #1 unblocks the
empirical end-to-end verification that motivates Fix #5's
documentation, (c) Fix #2 + #3 + #4 are all M6c CDC
operationalisation on the read side, structurally adjacent to
Fix #1's write-side restoration.

Structural remedy:

  - `framework/orchestrator/scripts/pos_session_start.py` —
    new `_maybe_reseat_stop_hook(loam_root)` helper; called from
    `main()` after `_maybe_install_status_line(loam_root)`.
  - `framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/
    memory_consumer.py:305-307` — Fix #2 empty-state string.
  - `framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/
    memory_consumer.py:243-264` — Fix #3 `_append_diag` exception
    log mirror.
  - `framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/
    memory_consumer.py` module docstring — Fix #5 group_id
    convention narrative.
  - `framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/
    context_composer.py:541-546` — Fix #4 skip-empty-contributors.

Test surface (5 new AC tests):

  - `framework/orchestrator/tests/test_AC_MPF_1_reseat_stop_hook.py`
  - `framework/primary-persona/tests/test_AC_MPF_2_render_retrieval_empty_state_visible.py`
  - `framework/primary-persona/tests/test_AC_MPF_3_memory_reads_log_on_exception.py`
  - `framework/primary-persona/tests/test_AC_MPF_4_serialise_turn_skips_empty_contributors.py`
  - `framework/primary-persona/tests/test_AC_MPF_5_turn_aggregator_writes_with_workspace_slug.py`

AC surface (AC.MPF.1..MPF.6 + AC.MPF.S):

  - AC.MPF.1: Stop hook re-seated on every session-start.
  - AC.MPF.2: empty-results path emits visible diagnostic.
  - AC.MPF.3: exception path appends to memory-reads.log.
  - AC.MPF.4: empty contributors skipped from contributor_outputs.
  - AC.MPF.5: TurnAggregator.close_turn writes with group_id=
    workspace_slug.
  - AC.MPF.6: operational round-trip via raw HTTP curl
    (manual; recorded in §14).
  - AC.MPF.S: seal-diff invariant — only paths under
    primary-persona/, orchestrator/, hands-off-lifecycle/,
    or universal-paths.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - D1 — Lift only `_maybe_merge_stop` (not all four siblings).
    Minimal-scope discipline; structural gap captured as HSF#3.
  - D2 — Import `_maybe_merge_stop` directly into
    `pos_session_start.py` (no new module). Mirrors
    `_maybe_install_status_line` shape verbatim.
  - D6 — Fix #5 is documentation + regression-prevention only.
    No source change — persona already writes/reads with
    `group_id=workspace_slug`; orphan `pos-v2_default` data is
    accepted as lost.

Out of scope (per plan §8):

  - FastMCP `group_ids` filter brokenness (HSF#1; surface as
    separate amendment if reproducible at build-time).
  - Lifting `_maybe_merge_user_prompt_submit` /
    `_maybe_merge_status_line` / `_maybe_merge_pre_tool_use`
    into the session-start re-seating surface (HSF#3; only Stop
    is empirically broken in pos3).
  - Read-side success logging in `memory-reads.log` (HSF#5;
    only exception logging in this amendment).
  - Direct edit of pos3's `.claude/settings.json` (HT-7;
    operator triggers re-seat by starting a new session).

BASELINE `e3e3e17` (current HEAD post-amendment-#94 §14 SHA
backfill). primary-persona's SEAL_COMMIT sidecar lands at the
seal SHA via `loam amend seal`. orchestrator's SEAL_COMMIT
sidecar advances correspondingly.

# M-FBM — file-based memory baseline (memory-substrate pivot)

2026-05-01. v0.1.0 publish-blocker per master plan
`oss-v0-1-0-publish.md` §5 + series master
`oss-v0-1-0-publish-memory-pivot.md`. Two-amendment series
replacing graphiti as v0.1.0 default memory substrate; M-GMP
(graphiti-memory plugin migration) defers to the v0.1.x lane
post-M12.

Empirical justification (per series master §1 + research):
1 retrievable episode after weeks; 216MB graphiti err.log at
plan-time; 4 sealed amendments today (#92/#94/#95/#96) didn't
fix reliability; sidecar crashed at 16:04:27 today under normal
workload; 3 of 4 RED-class graphiti surfaces unexercised by
persona's actual retrieval path; auto-memory MEMORY.md already
carries 24 hand-curated rules at zero infra cost. M-FBM removes
graphiti from v0.1.0 runtime; M-GMP relocates the source as a
plugin post-publish.

All six §11 decisions ruled to plan recommendations 2026-05-01:

  - D-Q.MFBM.1 — Episode shape: one markdown file per turn.
  - D-Q.MFBM.2 — Retrieval: layered grep + BM25 via sqlite-FTS5;
    no embedding index at v0.1.0.
  - D-Q.MFBM.3 — Memory dir:
    `<workspace>/workspace/.loam/memory/` (D.2-shape; sibling of
    `<workspace>/workspace/.pos/`; the plan recommended
    `<workspace>/.loam/memory/` aligned to M1b's pending rename;
    builder pivoted to the actual landed shape per the plan's
    D-Q.MFBM.3 builder-pivot clause — M1b has not landed at
    M-FBM dispatch time, and `<workspace>/workspace/.loam/`
    is the post-D.2 sibling-of-`.pos` path that survives M1b's
    future `.pos`→`.loam` rename without data move).
  - D-Q.MFBM.4 — Auto-memory orthogonal (no merge, no mirror).
  - D-Q.MFBM.5 — Both bootstrap.contributions +
    `loam.memory.providers` entry-point groups; M-FBM authors
    the `MemoryProvider` Protocol stub (zero runtime impact);
    M-GMP implements graphiti's provider against it.
  - D-Q.MFBM.6 — kuzu_db: discard with one-shot inspection
    script. Inspection result on pos3 at amendment time:
    kuzu_db = 2.9 MB, 0 episode_uuid byte-occurrences,
    episodes.json fixture record count = 34 (test fixture, not
    live data). Research §5 evidence confirmed; halt-trigger
    §9.8 does NOT fire.

