# v0.1.2 item 5 — ack-first persona contract amendment

2026-05-03. v0.1.2 item per `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-x-roadmap.md`
§2 v0.1.2 item 5 + §5 Decision B (hard rule with 5 explicit
triggers) + §8 method-decision register backfill.

Sub-plan: `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-2-ack-first-persona-contract.md`.
FIDRAFT entry: "Acknowledge-first on complex requests"
(`docs/rebuild/FUTURE_IDEAS_DRAFT.md` 2026-05-03; rationale +
composition with Telegram-only channel rule, pause-on-Telegram-
outage, summarize-and-surface-decisions, critical-thinking-on-
deviations).

Scope (per sub-plan §4 + §6): single-component fence on
`framework/primary-persona/`. Source edit adds a new operational-
rule subsection `### Acknowledge first on non-trivial requests`
under `## Operational rules` in the persona template prompt.md.
The rule lands as a hard rule (Decision B) with five explicit
triggers, the trivial-back-and-forth carve-out, the ack-shape
literal "got it — doing X", and the absence-as-observable-
violation framing (mirrors the swarming-corpus model-rationale
absence-as-violation pattern).

Decision B choice rationale (from v0.1.x roadmap §5):
discipline encoded as observable habit, not as structural
enforcement (no UserPromptSubmit hook). Hook implementation is
non-trivial — "complex thought" requires LLM judgment that hooks
don't have access to; the simpler hook would be "ack EVERY user
prompt submit" which is too noisy for trivial messages.
Persona-level discipline is the right first cut.

Composes with Surface #2 (in-band drift fix per
feedback_loose_AC_text_fix_AC_not_implementation): pre-existing
test_AC_O_1_six_operational_rule_sections_present asserted six
ops; live template carried seven (post-α "Lean on the corpus"
landed additively but the AC count was not widened in α). v0.1.2
item 5 widens 6→8 ops + 11→13 total in lock-step (composes
Decision B's new addition with the α drift fix). The
test_AC_alpha_6_L_eleven_sections_unchanged test was unaffected
(asserts presence not count; additive landing preserves AC.α.6).

AC surface (per sub-plan §4):

  - AC.VPC.5.1 — `### Acknowledge first on non-trivial requests`
    subsection landed under `## Operational rules` with all 5
    triggers, carve-out, ack-shape literal, and absence-as-
    violation framing present. Verified by new test file
    `test_AC_VPC_5_ack_first_rule.py` (6 tests, all passing).
  - AC.VPC.5.2 — `test_AC_O_1_six_operational_rule_sections_*`
    renamed to `..._eight_*` (8 ops); `test_AC_O_1_named_section_
    count_is_eleven` renamed to `..._is_thirteen` (5 traits + 8
    rules). Both tests' tuples + assertion messages updated;
    module docstring updated in lock-step. Verified by
