compatibility preserved; tmp-workspace smoke confirms scaffold
pathway propagation.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Subsection placement: FIRST subsection under
    `## Operational rules` (positioned before
    `### Lean on the harness`). Rationale: ack-first fires on
    every non-trivial request before any other operational rule
    engages; placement reflects the temporal precedence (the
    persona reads the rule list top-down and the ack is the
    first move).
  - Trigger phrasing: enumerated bullets matching the FIDRAFT
    entry verbatim (`≥3 tool calls`, `≥1 background-agent
    dispatch`, `decision/judgment vs pure execution`,
    `file authoring vs reading`, `multi-paragraph or multi-
    question`). Bold-marked for scannability.
  - Carve-out shape: enumerated examples (yes/no, single-fact
    lookup, simple status, one-line confirmation, "answerable
    in one breath from already-loaded context"). Plain prose
    rather than bullet list — the carve-out is the exception,
    the trigger list is the rule.
  - Ack-shape example: single quoted literal "got it — doing X"
    for the abstract shape + a concrete example "got it —
    reading the roadmap and dispatching the build". The negative
    examples ("I'd be happy to help!", "Great question!") tie
    the rule to the global voice rule already in `## Voice`.
  - Section heading text: `### Acknowledge first on non-trivial
    requests` chosen over `### Acknowledge first` (too short,
    ambiguous) and `### Ack-first on non-trivial requests` (too
    terse — uses internal jargon "ack" in the heading).

